# Change: G-D7 and D-G (repertoire plan: st-change-g-d7-d-g). An original chord-change study.
# Each half is a ladder that changes faster and faster: the home chord G held for two bars (one
# strum a bar), then a change every bar with two strums, every bar with four strums, and every
# two beats. First half: G (320003) with D7 (xx0212). Second half: the four-finger G (320033)
# with D (xx0232); finger 3 stays on string 2, fret 3 (D) for both chords. Strum D and D7 on
# strings 4 to 1 only. Keep the metronome on: the new chord lands on the beat even if the strum
# before it catches open strings.
title: Change: G-D7 and D-G
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original chord-change study
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: chord changes, strumming, metronome, guide finger
tempo: 72
time: 4/4
key: G

track: Your strum
role: rhythm
[G and D7]
| ^"One strum a bar" "G=320003" w D | D | ^"Two strums a bar" "D7=xx0212" h D D | "G=320003" D D |
| ^"Four strums a bar" "D7=xx0212" q D D D D | "G=320003" D D D D | ^"Change every two beats" "D7=xx0212" D D "G=320003" D D | "D7=xx0212" D D "G=320003" D D ||
[D and G]
| ^"Four-finger G: finger 3 stays for D" "G=320033" w D | D | "D=xx0232" h D D | "G=320033" D D |
| "D=xx0232" q D D D D | "G=320033" D D D D | "D=xx0232" D D "G=320033" D D | "D=xx0232" D D "G=320033" D D ||
